{
  "answer": "You can declare query parameters using the `Query` parameter annotation, and validate them using the `Regex` or `All` validators from Pydantic. \n\nExample:\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, Query\nfrom pydantic import Regex, All\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.get(\"/items/\")\nasync def read_items(q: str = Query(None, regex=\"^.{1,10}$\", description=\"Item name\")):\n    return {\"item_name\": q}\n```\nIn this example, the `q` parameter is declared as a query parameter with a regex validation.",
